      "id": 62,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**R = Real-Time Determinism.** The C0-state residency panel below is always live (from `intel_powerstat`). The **IPC / SMI / per-core** panels populate only when the opt-in turbostat reader is enabled (`ENABLE_TURBOSTAT=true`, requires the kernel-matched `linux-tools` package) \u2014 otherwise they read *No data*, which is expected. SMI (System Management Interrupts) are the #1 hidden cause of RT latency spikes."
      }
